<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu'l-Abbas Ma'mun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1017</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Ma'mun II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu'l-Abbas Ma'mun, Ma'mun II, was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmshah">Khwarazmshah</a> of the Ma'munid dynasty from 1009 to 1017, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurganj">Gurganj</a>. He continued his brother Ali's patronage of scholars, among them al-Biruni and, for a time, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avicenna">Ibn Sina</a>. Pressed by his brother-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a> to accept his overlordship, he was killed by his own troops in 1017, and Mahmud then conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a>.</p></div>
